.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.TH OCTA-CAPTURE-HTTP 1 "" "OCTA-CAPTURE @PROJECT_VERSION@" "OCTA-CAPTURE Manual"
.SH NAME
octa\-capture\-http \- serve the local OCTA-CAPTURE control panel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBocta-capture-http\fR [\fB\-\-port\fR PORT] [\fB\-\-open\fR]
                  [\fB\-\-bin-dir\fR DIR] [\fB\-\-midi-port\fR PORT]
                  [\fB\-\-data-dir\fR DIR] [\fB\-\-help\fR]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Serve the same panel as octa-capture(1), bound to 127.0.0.1.
The default HTTP port is 8765; port 0 chooses an unused port.
The printed private link includes the authentication token.
Keep this link private. The server checks request Host/Origin and control tokens,
and loads local assets.
.PP
The directory and MIDI options have the meanings documented in octa-capture(1).
The \fB\-\-open\fR option opens the private link in the default browser.
SIGINT or SIGTERM shuts down the server and releases its control connection.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success; nonzero indicates a usage, device or operation error.
.SH SEE ALSO
octa-capture(1), octa-status(1), octa-preset(1)
